 ENDF/B-VI MOD 1 Evaluation, November 1989, D. Larson (ORNL)      2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
   This work employed nuclear model codes including the           2431 1451
Distorted Wave Born Approximation (DWBA) program DWUCK [Ku72]     2431 1451
and the Hauser-Feshbach code TNG [Fu80,Fu88,Sh86].  The TNG code  2431 1451
provides energy and angular distributions of particles emitted    2431 1451
in the compound and pre-compound reactions, ensures consistency   2431 1451
among all reactions, and maintains energy balance. Details        2431 1451
pertinent to the contents of this evaluation and extensive        2431 1451
comparisons of calculations with experimental data can be found   2431 1451
in Hetrick [He87].                                                2431 1451
                                                                  2431 1451
DESCRIPTION OF FILES                                              2431 1451
(MF-MT)                                                           2431 1451
  1-451 GENERAL INFORMATION, REFERENCES, AND DEFINITIONS.         2431 1451
  2-151 RESONANCE PARAMETERS;  USED TO PROVIDE THE TOTAL AND      2431 1451
        SCATTERING CROSS SECTIONS FROM 1.E-5 EV TO 980 KEV, AND   2431 1451
        CAPTURE FROM 1.E-5 TO 375 KEV.  A SMALL CONTRIBUTION IN   2431 1451
        3-102 IS ADDED TO 2-151 FOR CAPTURE FROM 375 TO 980 KEV   2431 1451
        (SEE 3-102 BELOW).  THE RESONANCE PARAMETERS              2431 1451
        FROM [Br85] (WITH HELP FROM BRUSEGAN ET AL. (PRIVATE      2431 1451
        COMM., 1988)) WERE ADJUSTED TO MINIMIZE DIFFERENCE WITH   2431 1451
        DATA OF REF. [Ag84].                                      2431 1451
        NOTE THAT THE FLAG HAS BEEN SET TO ALLOW USER CALCULATION 2431 1451
        OF THE ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS FROM THE R-M RESONANCE       2431 1451
        PARAMETERS, IF THE USER WANTS ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ON    2431 1451
        A FINER ENERGY GRID THAN GIVEN IN 4/2.                    2431 1451
